1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,037
In this town, reflections go home at three o'clock.

2
00:00:04,027 --> 00:00:05,489
Every mirror goes blank.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:07,422
Every window. Every puddle.

4
00:00:07,893 --> 00:00:10,286
For one hour, nobody has a reflection.

5
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:14,946
Your reflection has its own house, its own job, its own friends.

6
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,934
They come back at four. Every single day.

7
00:00:19,827 --> 00:00:21,592
You've never thought about it.

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,016
Until today.

9
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,401
At four o'clock, everybody's reflection came back.

10
00:00:27,127 --> 00:00:27,983
Except yours.

11
00:00:28,927 --> 00:00:30,692
You waved at the mirror.

12
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,419
Nothing waved back.

13
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:35,431
Your mom looked at the empty mirror.

14
00:00:36,227 --> 00:00:37,386
Then at you.

15
00:00:38,027 --> 00:00:40,095
And slowly took a step back.

16
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,131
Because in this town, there's a saying.

17
00:00:43,927 --> 00:00:45,995
If your reflection doesn't come back...

18
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,728
it found someone it likes better.

19
00:00:49,393 --> 00:00:50,552
You started searching.

20
00:00:51,193 --> 00:00:53,262
The mirror maze at the fair.

21
00:00:53,927 --> 00:00:54,783
The lake.

22
00:00:55,727 --> 00:00:57,795
The shop windows on Main Street.

23
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,013
Nothing.

24
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:01,722
Then you saw it.

25
00:01:02,193 --> 00:01:05,171
In the window of the house across the street.

26
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,030
Your reflection.

27
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,725
Sitting at a dinner table.

28
00:01:10,293 --> 00:01:10,846
Laughing.

29
00:01:12,093 --> 00:01:14,162
With a family you've never met.

30
00:01:14,827 --> 00:01:15,986
It looked happy.

31
00:01:16,627 --> 00:01:18,392
Happier than you've ever looked.

32
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,119
It saw you.

33
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,919
It stopped laughing.

34
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,628
And it walked to the window.

35
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,665
It pressed its hand against the glass.

36
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,922
And mouthed three words.

37
00:01:30,393 --> 00:01:31,552
"Your turn now."

38
00:01:32,193 --> 00:01:33,958
Then the glass went soft.

39
00:01:34,527 --> 00:01:35,383
Like water.

40
00:01:36,327 --> 00:01:37,486
And it pulled.

